John Harris, who writes a column about roguelikes for Game Set Watch,
has written a few things about Shiren the Wanderer:

http://www.gamesetwatch.com/2008/03/play_the_delights_of_mystery_d.php
http://www.gamesetwatch.com/2007/07/play_journal_of_the_trip_to_ta.php

In the second one of those, he says that Shiren the Wanderer borrows
some features from NetHack -- vaults, shops with guards that are
summoned if you steal, scrolls of genocide, and blank scrolls you
can write on. (I've never played it though.)


